# CipherRoll rules for Cursor (native Swift)

## Project
- Native iOS app in Swift and SwiftUI, iOS 16+, universal (iPhone, iPad, iPhone Duo). Name CipherRoll. MVVM with `ObservableObject`. Layout: `App/`, `Features/<Name>/`, `Core/Crypto`, `Core/Storage`, `Core/Analytics`, `DesignSystem/`. Share Extension is its own target.
- Design source of truth: `docs/13_CipherRoll_Final_Screen_Manifest.md` and the PNGs in `design/screens/`. Never build a screen marked DO NOT BUILD. If a screen is missing, ask before inventing it.
- Tokens, copy and feature rules: `docs/11_CipherRoll_Developer_Handoff.md` (use `docs/00_Native_iOS_Stack.md` for the stack). Events: `docs/10`. Help text: `docs/09`.

## Security (highest priority)
- Items: CryptoKit `AES.GCM`, random 256-bit key per item, item key wrapped by a vault key, vault key wrapped by a key derived from the lock secret (PBKDF2 with high iterations, or Argon2id). Random salt per vault.
- Keys only in the Keychain (`WhenUnlockedThisDeviceOnly`) or derived on unlock. Zero out key material when done (`withUnsafeMutableBytes`, `memset_s`) and never keep keys in global state.
- Never write a readable copy of vault data to disk. Decrypt to memory, or to a protected temp file deleted on close and on app launch.
- Files: `.completeFileProtection`, `isExcludedFromBackup = true`.
- Import: copy, verify size or hash, then (only if the user agrees) offer to delete originals. Never delete before verify.
- Never log PINs, keys, file names, note text or search words. No `print` or `os_log` with user data.
- Decoy vault: separate store and key. Nothing (timing, logs, analytics) may show which vault opened.
- Hide the app-switcher preview. Lock on every return to the app.

## Product rules
- No ads, no ATT. No monthly plan. Trial UI only when StoreKit says the user is eligible.
- Never use "encrypted", "military-grade", "unhackable" in UI until Praba confirms the security gate passed. Use "Vault contents stay on this iPhone".
- Positive paywall copy. Show price, period, auto-renew text and "Cancel anytime in Settings".
- Analytics only after consent, behind an `Analytics` protocol (Mixpanel behind it). Buckets for counts. Never send content.

## UI rules
- Colours and sizes from doc 11 section 3. Text on gold is navy `#14233B`, never white.
- Manrope bundled, Phosphor Swift icons.
- Dynamic Type to accessibility sizes, VoiceOver labels on every icon button, 44x44 pt touch targets, Reduce Motion (120 to 180 ms fades via `@Environment(\.accessibilityReduceMotion)`).
- Light and dark mode both, matching the PNGs.

## Working style
- One phase at a time. After each phase: build, run tests, list what changed, stop for review.
- If docs and a PNG disagree: manifest wins, then doc 11. Ask Praba only product questions, in plain words.
- PIN: minimum 6 digits, never allow 4. Optional 8+ or alphanumeric. Recovery key covers real vaults only, never the decoy. Decoy has its own PIN and keys and no recovery.
- Do the Phase 0A security design documents before any vault code. Do not mark a security requirement complete without a passing reproducible test.
- No claim of forensic erasure anywhere in code, copy or docs.
- Devices: one universal app. Adaptive SwiftUI layouts only: size classes, no `UIScreen.main`, no fixed widths or device-model checks. iPad regular width uses a sidebar split view; sheets are centered. iPhone Duo open behaves like iPad, closed like iPhone; never require folding; keep state through a fold. Read `LAContext.biometryType` instead of hardcoding "Face ID". See doc 11 section 10 and `design/screens/10_iPad_and_Duo`.
- iPhone Duo: build with Xcode 27.1 and the iOS 27.1 SDK or later. Use standard TabView, toolbars and NavigationSplitView so the vertical bar and sidebars move on their own; every tab needs a title and an icon. Handle each safe-area edge separately. Posture changes must not reload content or lose scroll position. See `design/screens/11_iPhone_Duo`.
